{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pu4CbDCMXBDsneV2XjQVsa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: C1 软化：不声称 evidence 质量 competitive with encoder SOTA，改为 'generative\n2\t  LLM 首次实现 end-to-end evidence production，质量可用但在句子级对齐评估下与 discriminative 方法有 gap'。C2\n3\t  不变。C3 保留但 CED 从 recommended solution 降级为 one effective scoring function。C4 加 caveat：EDCR\n4\t  shows moderate human correlation; further validation needed。C5 保留。论文重心转向分析贡献：decoupling\n5\t  spectrum + scaling analysis 成为主卖点，RSFT 降为 sufficient solution enabling the analysis。\n6\timagined_experiments:\n7\t- name: Test Set Evaluation (RSFT CED best + no-evidence + SFT baseline)\n8\t  plan_id: plan_002\n9\t  description: 用 RSFT CED best config (s44) 和 SFT no-evidence 在 DocRED test set 上评估。本地计算\n10\t    Evi-F1、EDCR；同时计算 DREEAM-protocol Evi-F1（句子级 exact match）对比 DREEAM baseline。\n11\t  expected_results:\n12\t    test_ign_f1_rsft_ced_s44: 42.5\n13\t    test_f1_rsft_ced_s44: 43.3\n14\t    test_evi_f1_conditional_rsft: 0.798\n15\t    test_edcr_rsft: 0.665\n16\t    test_ign_f1_no_evidence: 45.5\n17\t    test_f1_no_evidence: 46.8\n18\t    test_evidence_tax_4b: -3.0\n19\t    test_ign_f1_sft_baseline: 38.2\n20\t    test_evi_f1_sft: 0.785\n21\t    dreeam_protocol_evi_f1_rsft: 0.42\n22\t    dreeam_protocol_evi_f1_sft: 0.38\n23\t    dreeam_baseline_evi_f1: 0.5401\n24\t    delta_vs_dreeam: -0.12\n25\t    test_dev_degradation_rsft: -3.35\n26\t    test_dev_degradation_no_evidence: -1.86\n27\t  result_rationale: Dev→test 退化来源于三个因素：(1) DocRED test set 标注质量略低于 dev（更多 distant\n28\t    supervision noise），RSFT 对 evidence quality 的依赖放大了这一影响；(2) RSFT 在 dev 上 seed variance\n29\t    已有 2.2pp（s42=43.63 vs s43=45.85），说明模型对数据分布敏感，test 分布偏移进一步放大；(3) no-evidence 模型退化较小（-1.86pp）因为它不承担\n30\t    evidence generation 的额外负担，对标注噪声更鲁棒。DREEAM-protocol Evi-F1 大幅低于 conditional evi_f1（0.42\n31\t    vs 0.80）是因为 DREEAM 协议做句子级 exact set match——FREIGE 的 evidence 是 generative production（LLM\n32\t    可能生成语义正确但句子边界不对齐的 evidence），而 DREEAM 是 discriminative retrieval（直接分类句子 ID），后者天然对齐句子级评估。0.42\n33\t    vs DREEAM 的 0.54 差距约 12pp，足以说明 generative approach 在 sentence-level alignment\n34\t    上有 gap，但 0.42 仍是非平凡的（远高于 random baseline ~0.15），证明 LLM 确实学到了 evidence grounding\n35\t    能力。Evidence tax 在 test 上从 dev 的 -1.5pp 扩大至 -3.0pp，因为 test 的 harder examples 让\n36\t    evidence generation 负担更重——模型容量在 harder distribution 上更紧张。\n37\t  tables:\n38\t  - name: 'Table: Test Set Main Results'\n39\t    columns:\n40\t    - Config\n41\t    - Ign-F1\n42\t    - F1\n43\t    - Evi-F1 (cond)\n44\t    - EDCR\n45\t    - DREEAM-proto Evi-F1\n46\t    rows:\n47\t    - - SFT no-evidence\n48\t      - '45.5'\n49\t      - '46.8'\n50\t      - —\n51\t      - —\n52\t      - —\n53\t    - - SFT baseline\n54\t      - '38.2'\n55\t      - '39.0'\n56\t      - '78.50'\n57\t      - '0.725'\n58\t      - '0.38'\n59\t    - - RSFT CED (best)\n60\t      - '42.5'\n61\t      - '43.3'\n62\t      - '79.80'\n63\t      - '0.665'\n64\t      - '0.42'\n65\t    - - DREEAM (RoBERTa-large)\n66\t      - 61.7*\n67\t      - 63.6*\n68\t      - —\n69\t      - —\n70\t      - '54.01'\n71\t    note: '*DREEAM 数字为 dev set（test 需 CodaLab），仅 Evi-F1 可直接对比'\n72\t  - name: 'Table: Dev→Test Degradation'\n73\t    columns:\n74\t    - Config\n75\t    - Dev Ign-F1\n76\t    - Test Ign-F1\n77\t    - Δ\n78\t    rows:\n79\t    - - RSFT CED best\n80\t      - '45.85'\n81\t      - '42.5'\n82\t      - '-3.35'\n83\t    - - SFT no-evidence\n84\t      - '47.36'\n85\t      - '45.5'\n86\t      - '-1.86'\n87\t    - - SFT baseline\n88\t      - '40.36'\n89\t      - '38.2'\n90\t      - '-2.16'\n91\t  figures_description:\n92\t  - 'Bar chart: Dev vs Test performance comparison across all configs, highlighting\n93\t    evidence tax expansion on test set'\n94\t  - 'Scatter plot: DREEAM-protocol Evi-F1 vs conditional Evi-F1, showing generative-discriminative\n95\t    gap'\n96\t  analysis: Test set 结果验证核心发现成立：RSFT 仍显著优于 SFT baseline（+4.3pp Ign-F1），evidence generation\n97\t    能力保持（evi_f1~0.80）。但 claim 强度需下调：(1) evidence tax 在 test 上扩大至 -3.0pp（dev 仅 -1.5pp），说明\n98\t    evidence generation burden 在 harder distribution 上更明显；(2) DREEAM-protocol Evi-F1\n99\t    仅 0.42，与 DREEAM 的 0.54 有 12pp gap——不能声称 competitive with encoder SOTA，只能说 'first\n100\t    generative approach to achieve non-trivial evidence grounding'；(3) dev-test degradation\n101\t    不均匀（RSFT 退化最大 -3.35pp），暗示 RSFT 可能轻度 overfit dev distribution。论文需显式报告并讨论这些 degradation，Claim\n102\t    1 叙事从 'evidence grounding comes at acceptable cost' 调整为 'evidence grounding is\n103\t    achievable but with scale-dependent and distribution-dependent costs'。\n104\t- name: Re-DocRED Cross-Dataset RSFT Pipeline\n105\t  plan_id: plan_007\n106\t  description: 在 Re-DocRED 上完成完整 RSFT pipeline：(1) 用 DocRED-trained SFT 模型在 Re-DocRED\n107\t    train 上生成 candidates，(2) CED scoring 筛选，(3) RSFT 训练，(4) Re-DocRED dev eval。验证\n108\t    RSFT 增益是否跨数据集泛化。注：Re-DocRED ~55% triples 无 evidence 标注。\n109\t  expected_results:\n110\t    redocred_rsft_ign_f1: 38.8\n111\t    redocred_rsft_f1: 39.4\n112\t    redocred_rsft_evi_f1: 0.822\n113\t    redocred_rsft_edcr: 0.655\n114\t    redocred_sft_ign_f1: 36.59\n115\t    redocred_rsft_delta_vs_sft: 2.2\n116\t    docred_rsft_delta_vs_sft: 5.49\n117\t    rsft_generalization_ratio: 0.4\n118\t    ced_scoring_selection_rate: 0.09\n119\t    ced_scoring_mean_f1: 0.55\n120\t    rsft_training_samples: 1800\n121\t  result_rationale: RSFT 增益从 DocRED 的 +5.49pp 缩减至 Re-DocRED 的 +2.2pp（generalization\n122\t    ratio 40%），原因：(1) CED scoring 依赖 NLI 模型对 evidence 质量的判断，但 Re-DocRED 的标注与 DocRED\n123\t    有系统性差异（Re-DocRED 修正了 DocRED 的 false negatives，relation 分布不同），导致 CED 在 Re-DocRED\n124\t    candidates 上的 discrimination power 下降——选出的训练数据质量低于 DocRED 场景（mean_f1 从 0.62 降至\n125\t    0.55）；(2) Re-DocRED 55% triples 无 evidence 标注意味着 CED 的 gold evidence overlap signal\n126\t    更 noisy（更多 'false negative' evidence），selection rate 从 12.4% 降至 ~9%，训练集更小；(3)\n127\t    SFT 本身在 Re-DocRED 上已退化 3.15pp（跨数据集 distribution shift），RSFT 在此 weaker base 上的\n128\t    marginal gain 自然更小。但 evi_f1 保持高位（0.822）证明 evidence extraction 能力的跨数据集泛化不受影响——RSFT\n129\t    的 evidence quality improvement 主要是 format/style alignment 而非 dataset-specific\n130\t    knowledge。\n131\t  tables:\n132\t  - name: 'Table: Re-DocRED Cross-Dataset Results'\n133\t    columns:\n134\t    - Config\n135\t    - Ign-F1\n136\t    - Evi-F1\n137\t    - EDCR\n138\t    - Δ vs SFT\n139\t    rows:\n140\t    - - SFT (zero-shot transfer)\n141\t      - '36.59'\n142\t      - '0.817'\n143\t      - '0.667'\n144\t      - —\n145\t    - - RSFT CED (Re-DocRED)\n146\t      - '38.8'\n147\t      - '0.822'\n148\t      - '0.655'\n149\t      - +2.2pp\n150\t    - - DocRED RSFT CED (reference)\n151\t      - '45.85'\n152\t      - '0.816'\n153\t      - '0.639'\n154\t      - +5.49pp\n155\t    note: Re-DocRED eval 使用 evidence_only mode（仅 43% triples 有标注）\n156\t  - name: 'Table: RSFT Generalization Gap'\n157\t    columns:\n158\t    - Dataset\n159\t    - RSFT Δ Ign-F1\n160\t    - CED selection rate\n161\t    - Training samples\n162\t    rows:\n163\t    - - DocRED\n164\t      - '+5.49'\n165\t      - 12.4%\n166\t      - '2718'\n167\t    - - Re-DocRED\n168\t      - '+2.2'\n169\t      - ~9%\n170\t      - ~1800\n171\t  figures_description:\n172\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: SFT→RSFT improvement on DocRED vs Re-DocRED, showing generalization\n173\t    gap'\n174\t  analysis: Re-DocRED 实验证实 RSFT 增益跨数据集存在但衰减显著（40% generalization ratio）。两个积极信号：(1)\n175\t    evi_f1 跨数据集保持 0.82+，evidence extraction 是 transferable skill；(2) EDCR 改善方向一致（0.667→0.655）。但\n176\t    rel_f1 增益缩减说明 CED scoring 的 domain-specific effectiveness 有限——它依赖于训练分布下的 evidence\n177\t    pattern，跨数据集需要 recalibration。论文叙事：Re-DocRED 作为 robustness check 报告，承认 RSFT 增益\n178\t    partially dataset-specific，但 evidence production capability 本身泛化良好。\n179\t- name: EDCR Human Annotation Validation\n180\t  plan_id: plan_013\n181\t  description: 100 个样本人工标注验证：从 RSFT CED best 输出中采样 100 个 (triple, evidence) pairs，人工判断\n182\t    evidence 是否真正支持对应 relation。计算 EDCR 与人工判断的 Spearman correlation。\n183\t  expected_results:\n184\t    n_annotated: 100\n185\t    human_agreement_rate: 0.72\n186\t    edcr_human_spearman_rho: 0.55\n187\t    edcr_human_spearman_p: 0.001\n188\t    edcr_human_pearson_r: 0.48\n189\t    human_evi_f1_correlation: 0.35\n190\t    inter_annotator_agreement_kappa: 0.65\n191\t    annotation_categories:\n192\t      fully_supported: 58\n193\t      partially_supported: 22\n194\t      not_supported: 12\n195\t      ambiguous: 8\n196\t    edcr_precision_at_high: 0.7\n197\t    edcr_precision_at_low: 0.45\n198\t  result_rationale: EDCR 与人工判断达到 moderate correlation（ρ=0.55）而非 strong correlation，原因：(1)\n199\t    EDCR 基于 NLI entailment probability，但 NLI 模型对 DocRE 域的 evidence 关系理解有局限——某些 relation\n200\t    types（如 temporal、geographic）的 evidence 需要多跳推理，NLI 模型会给出 neutral 判断，而人类会判为 supported；(2)\n201\t    EDCR 的 contrastive design 比较 gold evidence vs distractor 的 NLI 差值，但人工标注是 absolute\n202\t    judgment（是否支持），两种 operationalization 有 systematic gap；(3) per-relation analysis\n203\t    已显示 EDCR 与 evi_f1 几乎正交（ρ=-0.064），说明 EDCR 捕捉的维度与传统 evidence quality 不同，人工标注可能更接近\n204\t    evi_f1 的语义（表面匹配），导致 EDCR-human 相关度受限。高 EDCR 端（>0.8，病理模型）precision 达 0.70（识别 'bad\n205\t    evidence' 较准），但低 EDCR 端（<0.5，good models）precision 仅 0.45——说明 EDCR 更擅长诊断极端病理案例，对\n206\t    fine-grained quality ranking 能力有限。\n207\t  tables:\n208\t  - name: 'Table: EDCR Human Validation Summary'\n209\t    columns:\n210\t    - Metric\n211\t    - Value\n212\t    - Interpretation\n213\t    rows:\n214\t    - - Spearman ρ (EDCR vs human)\n215\t      - '0.55'\n216\t      - Moderate positive correlation\n217\t    - - p-value\n218\t      - <0.001\n219\t      - Statistically significant\n220\t    - - Human agreement (fully/partially supported)\n221\t      - 80%\n222\t      - Evidence generally useful\n223\t    - - EDCR precision at pathological range\n224\t      - '0.70'\n225\t      - Good diagnostic for failure modes\n226\t    - - EDCR precision at healthy range\n227\t      - '0.45'\n228\t      - Limited fine-grained discrimination\n229\t  - name: 'Table: Human Annotation Distribution'\n230\t    columns:\n231\t    - Category\n232\t    - Count\n233\t    - Proportion\n234\t    rows:\n235\t    - - Fully supported\n236\t      - '58'\n237\t      - 58%\n238\t    - - Partially supported\n239\t      - '22'\n240\t      - 22%\n241\t    - - Not supported\n242\t      - '12'\n243\t      - 12%\n244\t    - - Ambiguous\n245\t      - '8'\n246\t      - 8%\n247\t  figures_description:\n248\t  - 'Scatter plot: EDCR score vs human support rating (4-point scale), with regression\n249\t    line and confidence band'\n250\t  - 'Confusion matrix: EDCR binary prediction (threshold=0.7) vs human binary judgment\n251\t    (supported vs not)'\n252\t  analysis: ρ=0.55 支持 EDCR 作为有意义的诊断指标，但不足以声称 'validated automatic metric'。关键发现：EDCR\n253\t    在方法级诊断（区分 catastrophic vs healthy models）的有效性远高于 sample 级 fine-grained ranking。论文需加\n254\t    caveat：'EDCR demonstrates moderate correlation with human judgments (ρ=0.55, p<0.001),\n255\t    providing useful method-level diagnostics while acknowledging limitations in instance-level\n256\t    precision. Further large-scale validation is needed before EDCR can serve as a\n257\t    standalone evaluation metric.' Claim 4 的 Layer 1（方法级）不受影响——EDCR vs rel_f1 的 ρ=-0.965\n258\t    是纯数值关系，不依赖人工验证。Layer 2（per-relation 诊断）需要 qualified：'EDCR reveals relation-type\n259\t    difficulty patterns that merit further human validation.'\n260\t- name: NLI Model Ablation (DeBERTa-base vs large)\n261\t  plan_id: plan_010\n262\t  description: 用 DeBERTa-v3-base 替代 DeBERTa-v3-large 作为 CED scorer，重新打分 RSFT candidates\n263\t    并训练，对比 RSFT 质量差异。验证 NLI 模型能力对 CED scoring quality 的影响。\n264\t  expected_results:\n265\t    base_ced_discrimination_accuracy: 0.755\n266\t    large_ced_discrimination_accuracy: 0.815\n267\t    base_rsft_ign_f1: 44.1\n268\t    large_rsft_ign_f1: 45.0\n269\t    base_rsft_rel_f1: 0.448\n270\t    large_rsft_rel_f1: 0.4569\n271\t    base_rsft_evi_f1: 0.805\n272\t    large_rsft_evi_f1: 0.8143\n273\t    delta_ign_f1: -0.9\n274\t    delta_rel_f1: -0.0089\n275\t    base_selection_rate: 0.135\n276\t    large_selection_rate: 0.124\n277\t    base_mean_ced_score: 0.625\n278\t    large_mean_ced_score: 0.668\n279\t  result_rationale: DeBERTa-v3-base 比 large 参数少 60%（184M vs 434M），NLI accuracy 从 ~91%\n280\t    降至 ~88%（MNLI benchmark）。这导致 CED scoring 的 discrimination accuracy 从 0.815 降至 0.755——base\n281\t    模型在 subtle evidence distinctions（需要深层语义理解的 cases）上给出更多 false positives，selection\n282\t    threshold 下 base 选出更多但质量更低的 samples（selection rate 略高 13.5% vs 12.4%）。传导至 RSFT\n283\t    训练：base-scored 数据中混入更多 borderline/noisy samples，最终 RSFT 模型退化约 0.9pp Ign-F1。这个差距存在但不大（不足\n284\t    1pp），原因是 CED 的 contrastive design 本身有 robustness——即使 absolute NLI scores 不准确，gold\n285\t    vs distractor 的 relative ordering 在 base model 下仍大部分保持。结论：NLI model quality matters\n286\t    but is not the dominant factor——CED 的 contrastive margin 设计提供了对 NLI model imperfection\n287\t    的一定鲁棒性。这支持 Claim 3 的 'NLI-based scoring 是关键' 叙事（即使用 weaker NLI model 仍有效）。\n288\t  tables:\n289\t  - name: 'Table: NLI Model Ablation'\n290\t    columns:\n291\t    - NLI Model\n292\t    - Params\n293\t    - CED Discrim. Acc\n294\t    - RSFT Ign-F1\n295\t    - RSFT rel_f1\n296\t    - RSFT evi_f1\n297\t    rows:\n298\t    - - DeBERTa-v3-large\n299\t      - 434M\n300\t      - '0.815'\n301\t      - '45.0'\n302\t      - '0.4569'\n303\t      - '0.8143'\n304\t    - - DeBERTa-v3-base\n305\t      - 184M\n306\t      - '0.755'\n307\t      - '44.1'\n308\t      - '0.4480'\n309\t      - '0.8050'\n310\t    - - Δ (base - large)\n311\t      - —\n312\t      - '-0.060'\n313\t      - -0.9pp\n314\t      - '-0.0089'\n315\t      - '-0.0093'\n316\t    note: large 为 3-seed mean (CED RSFT s42/s44)，base 为 1-seed estimate\n317\t  figures_description:\n318\t  - 'Bar chart: CED discrimination accuracy and downstream RSFT performance for base\n319\t    vs large NLI model'\n320\t  analysis: NLI model ablation 在 median 档下为 Claim 3 提供补充而非关键证据。base 模型仍能产出有效的 RSFT\n321\t    训练数据（rel_f1=0.448 仍显著优于 SFT baseline 0.405），但优势缩减约 1pp。作为 P2 ablation 放入附录即可——主要结论是\n322\t    CED 的 contrastive design 对 NLI model quality 有一定 tolerance，但 stronger NLI model\n323\t    still helps。不影响核心 claims。\n324\t- name: Post-hoc Evidence Retrieval Baseline (SFT + BM25)\n325\t  plan_id: post_hoc_retrieval\n326\t  description: 用 SFT no-evidence 模型抽取 relations，再用 BM25 从文档中 retrieve evidence sentences。对比\n327\t    RSFT 端到端方案的 evidence 质量。验证 post-hoc retrieval 是否为更简单的替代方案。\n328\t  expected_results:\n329\t    posthoc_rel_f1: 0.4893\n330\t    posthoc_ign_f1: 0.4736\n331\t    posthoc_evi_f1_bm25: 0.74\n332\t    posthoc_edcr: 0.58\n333\t    rsft_best_evi_f1: 0.8156\n334\t    rsft_best_rel_f1: 0.4683\n335\t    delta_evi_f1_vs_rsft: -0.076\n336\t    delta_rel_f1_vs_rsft: 0.021\n337\t    bm25_recall_at_3: 0.82\n338\t    bm25_precision_at_3: 0.55\n339\t  result_rationale: Post-hoc retrieval 的 rel_f1 等于 SFT no-evidence（0.4893）因为 relation\n340\t    extraction 与 evidence retrieval 完全解耦——这是其最大优势（无 evidence tax）也是最大弱点。BM25 evidence\n341\t    retrieval 达到 evi_f1=0.74，原因：(1) DocRE 的 evidence sentences 通常包含 head/tail entity\n342\t    mention，BM25 的 term matching 能有效定位这些句子；(2) 但 BM25 无法处理需要推理的 evidence（entity 未直接出现在\n343\t    evidence sentence 中的 cases），这类约占 25-30%。evi_f1=0.74 vs RSFT 的 0.82——差距约 8pp，处于\n344\t    median tier 定义的 '差距不够显著(<10pp)' 范围。这削弱了 RSFT 端到端方案的不可替代性叙事：一个简单的 two-stage pipeline（better\n345\t    extraction + BM25 retrieval）在 rel_f1 上更高（+2.1pp，因无 evidence tax）且 evidence quality\n346\t    差距有限。但 post-hoc 方案的 EDCR 为 0.58（高于 RSFT 的 0.64），说明 BM25 retrieved evidence 虽然\n347\t    token overlap 高但 faithfulness 更差——它检索的是 'relevant' 而非 'supporting' sentences。\n348\t  tables:\n349\t  - name: 'Table: End-to-end vs Post-hoc Comparison'\n350\t    columns:\n351\t    - Approach\n352\t    - rel_f1\n353\t    - Evi-F1\n354\t    - EDCR\n355\t    - Total Latency\n356\t    rows:\n357\t    - - RSFT CED (end-to-end)\n358\t      - '0.4683'\n359\t      - '0.816'\n360\t      - '0.639'\n361\t      - 1x\n362\t    - - SFT no-evi + BM25 (post-hoc)\n363\t      - '0.4893'\n364\t      - '0.740'\n365\t      - '0.580'\n366\t      - 1.2x\n367\t    - - CED reranker (N=8)\n368\t      - '0.4864'\n369\t      - '0.819'\n370\t      - '0.616'\n371\t      - 8x\n372\t    note: Post-hoc rel_f1 更高因为无 evidence generation burden\n373\t  figures_description:\n374\t  - 'Radar chart: end-to-end vs post-hoc on 4 axes (rel_f1, evi_f1, EDCR, efficiency)'\n375\t  analysis: Post-hoc baseline 是 median 档下最具威胁的对比实验。它暴露了 RSFT 端到端方案的核心张力：为了 jointly\n376\t    produce evidence 付出了 rel_f1 代价（-2.1pp vs no-evidence），获得的 evidence quality 优势仅\n377\t    +7.6pp evi_f1。论文应对策略：(1) 强调 EDCR 差异——RSFT 的 evidence 更 faithful（EDCR 0.64 vs 0.58），不只是表面\n378\t    overlap；(2) 指出 post-hoc approach 无法保证 evidence-relation consistency（retrieve 到的\n379\t    evidence 可能支持文档中其他 relation 而非 predicted one）；(3) 将 comparison 框架为 'trade-off\n380\t    analysis' 而非 'RSFT wins'——端到端方案在 faithfulness 上有优势，two-stage 在 extraction accuracy\n381\t    上有优势，choice depends on application requirements。Claim 1 不再能声称端到端方案不可替代，需调整为 'one\n382\t    effective approach with unique faithfulness properties'。\n383\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6526ddff-52fc-4cef-8b69-9b7b77bf8489","uuid":"f4d5a1c7-62ec-44c3-adc3-7e92181fc6cb","timestamp":"2026-05-16T16:26:21.530Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_6/projects/faith-evidence-ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T155803/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: C1 软化：不声称 evidence 质量 competitive with encoder SOTA，改为 'generative\n  LLM 首次实现 end-to-end evidence production，质量可用但在句子级对齐评估下与 discriminative 方法有 gap'。C2\n  不变。C3 保留但 CED 从 recommended solution 降级为 one effective scoring function。C4 加 caveat：EDCR\n  shows moderate human correlation; further validation needed。C5 保留。论文重心转向分析贡献：decoupling\n  spectrum + scaling analysis 成为主卖点，RSFT 降为 sufficient solution enabling the analysis。\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Test Set Evaluation (RSFT CED best + no-evidence + SFT baseline)\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 用 RSFT CED best config (s44) 和 SFT no-evidence 在 DocRED test set 上评估。本地计算\n    Evi-F1、EDCR；同时计算 DREEAM-protocol Evi-F1（句子级 exact match）对比 DREEAM baseline。\n  expected_results:\n    test_ign_f1_rsft_ced_s44: 42.5\n    test_f1_rsft_ced_s44: 43.3\n    test_evi_f1_conditional_rsft: 0.798\n    test_edcr_rsft: 0.665\n    test_ign_f1_no_evidence: 45.5\n    test_f1_no_evidence: 46.8\n    test_evidence_tax_4b: -3.0\n    test_ign_f1_sft_baseline: 38.2\n    test_evi_f1_sft: 0.785\n    dreeam_protocol_evi_f1_rsft: 0.42\n    dreeam_protocol_evi_f1_sft: 0.38\n    dreeam_baseline_evi_f1: 0.5401\n    delta_vs_dreeam: -0.12\n    test_dev_degradation_rsft: -3.35\n    test_dev_degradation_no_evidence: -1.86\n  result_rationale: Dev→test 退化来源于三个因素：(1) DocRED test set 标注质量略低于 dev（更多 distant\n    supervision noise），RSFT 对 evidence quality 的依赖放大了这一影响；(2) RSFT 在 dev 上 seed variance\n    已有 2.2pp（s42=43.63 vs s43=45.85），说明模型对数据分布敏感，test 分布偏移进一步放大；(3) no-evidence 模型退化较小（-1.86pp）因为它不承担\n    evidence generation 的额外负担，对标注噪声更鲁棒。DREEAM-protocol Evi-F1 大幅低于 conditional evi_f1（0.42\n    vs 0.80）是因为 DREEAM 协议做句子级 exact set match——FREIGE 的 evidence 是 generative production（LLM\n    可能生成语义正确但句子边界不对齐的 evidence），而 DREEAM 是 discriminative retrieval（直接分类句子 ID），后者天然对齐句子级评估。0.42\n    vs DREEAM 的 0.54 差距约 12pp，足以说明 generative approach 在 sentence-level alignment\n    上有 gap，但 0.42 仍是非平凡的（远高于 random baseline ~0.15），证明 LLM 确实学到了 evidence grounding\n    能力。Evidence tax 在 test 上从 dev 的 -1.5pp 扩大至 -3.0pp，因为 test 的 harder examples 让\n    evidence generation 负担更重——模型容量在 harder distribution 上更紧张。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Test Set Main Results'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - Ign-F1\n    - F1\n    - Evi-F1 (cond)\n    - EDCR\n    - DREEAM-proto Evi-F1\n    rows:\n    - - SFT no-evidence\n      - '45.5'\n      - '46.8'\n      - —\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - SFT baseline\n      - '38.2'\n      - '39.0'\n      - '78.50'\n      - '0.725'\n      - '0.38'\n    - - RSFT CED (best)\n      - '42.5'\n      - '43.3'\n      - '79.80'\n      - '0.665'\n      - '0.42'\n    - - DREEAM (RoBERTa-large)\n      - 61.7*\n      - 63.6*\n      - —\n      - —\n      - '54.01'\n    note: '*DREEAM 数字为 dev set（test 需 CodaLab），仅 Evi-F1 可直接对比'\n  - name: 'Table: Dev→Test Degradation'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - Dev Ign-F1\n    - Test Ign-F1\n    - Δ\n    rows:\n    - - RSFT CED best\n      - '45.85'\n      - '42.5'\n      - '-3.35'\n    - - SFT no-evidence\n      - '47.36'\n      - '45.5'\n      - '-1.86'\n    - - SFT baseline\n      - '40.36'\n      - '38.2'\n      - '-2.16'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: Dev vs Test performance comparison across all configs, highlighting\n    evidence tax expansion on test set'\n  - 'Scatter plot: DREEAM-protocol Evi-F1 vs conditional Evi-F1, showing generative-discriminative\n    gap'\n  analysis: Test set 结果验证核心发现成立：RSFT 仍显著优于 SFT baseline（+4.3pp Ign-F1），evidence generation\n    能力保持（evi_f1~0.80）。但 claim 强度需下调：(1) evidence tax 在 test 上扩大至 -3.0pp（dev 仅 -1.5pp），说明\n    evidence generation burden 在 harder distribution 上更明显；(2) DREEAM-protocol Evi-F1\n    仅 0.42，与 DREEAM 的 0.54 有 12pp gap——不能声称 competitive with encoder SOTA，只能说 'first\n    generative approach to achieve non-trivial evidence grounding'；(3) dev-test degradation\n    不均匀（RSFT 退化最大 -3.35pp），暗示 RSFT 可能轻度 overfit dev distribution。论文需显式报告并讨论这些 degradation，Claim\n    1 叙事从 'evidence grounding comes at acceptable cost' 调整为 'evidence grounding is\n    achievable but with scale-dependent and distribution-dependent costs'。\n- name: Re-DocRED Cross-Dataset RSFT Pipeline\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 在 Re-DocRED 上完成完整 RSFT pipeline：(1) 用 DocRED-trained SFT 模型在 Re-DocRED\n    train 上生成 candidates，(2) CED scoring 筛选，(3) RSFT 训练，(4) Re-DocRED dev eval。验证\n    RSFT 增益是否跨数据集泛化。注：Re-DocRED ~55% triples 无 evidence 标注。\n  expected_results:\n    redocred_rsft_ign_f1: 38.8\n    redocred_rsft_f1: 39.4\n    redocred_rsft_evi_f1: 0.822\n    redocred_rsft_edcr: 0.655\n    redocred_sft_ign_f1: 36.59\n    redocred_rsft_delta_vs_sft: 2.2\n    docred_rsft_delta_vs_sft: 5.49\n    rsft_generalization_ratio: 0.4\n    ced_scoring_selection_rate: 0.09\n    ced_scoring_mean_f1: 0.55\n    rsft_training_samples: 1800\n  result_rationale: RSFT 增益从 DocRED 的 +5.49pp 缩减至 Re-DocRED 的 +2.2pp（generalization\n    ratio 40%），原因：(1) CED scoring 依赖 NLI 模型对 evidence 质量的判断，但 Re-DocRED 的标注与 DocRED\n    有系统性差异（Re-DocRED 修正了 DocRED 的 false negatives，relation 分布不同），导致 CED 在 Re-DocRED\n    candidates 上的 discrimination power 下降——选出的训练数据质量低于 DocRED 场景（mean_f1 从 0.62 降至\n    0.55）；(2) Re-DocRED 55% triples 无 evidence 标注意味着 CED 的 gold evidence overlap signal\n    更 noisy（更多 'false negative' evidence），selection rate 从 12.4% 降至 ~9%，训练集更小；(3)\n    SFT 本身在 Re-DocRED 上已退化 3.15pp（跨数据集 distribution shift），RSFT 在此 weaker base 上的\n    marginal gain 自然更小。但 evi_f1 保持高位（0.822）证明 evidence extraction 能力的跨数据集泛化不受影响——RSFT\n    的 evidence quality improvement 主要是 format/style alignment 而非 dataset-specific\n    knowledge。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Re-DocRED Cross-Dataset Results'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - Ign-F1\n    - Evi-F1\n    - EDCR\n    - Δ vs SFT\n    rows:\n    - - SFT (zero-shot transfer)\n      - '36.59'\n      - '0.817'\n      - '0.667'\n      - —\n    - - RSFT CED (Re-DocRED)\n      - '38.8'\n      - '0.822'\n      - '0.655'\n      - +2.2pp\n    - - DocRED RSFT CED (reference)\n      - '45.85'\n      - '0.816'\n      - '0.639'\n      - +5.49pp\n    note: Re-DocRED eval 使用 evidence_only mode（仅 43% triples 有标注）\n  - name: 'Table: RSFT Generalization Gap'\n    columns:\n    - Dataset\n    - RSFT Δ Ign-F1\n    - CED selection rate\n    - Training samples\n    rows:\n    - - DocRED\n      - '+5.49'\n      - 12.4%\n      - '2718'\n    - - Re-DocRED\n      - '+2.2'\n      - ~9%\n      - ~1800\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: SFT→RSFT improvement on DocRED vs Re-DocRED, showing generalization\n    gap'\n  analysis: Re-DocRED 实验证实 RSFT 增益跨数据集存在但衰减显著（40% generalization ratio）。两个积极信号：(1)\n    evi_f1 跨数据集保持 0.82+，evidence extraction 是 transferable skill；(2) EDCR 改善方向一致（0.667→0.655）。但\n    rel_f1 增益缩减说明 CED scoring 的 domain-specific effectiveness 有限——它依赖于训练分布下的 evidence\n    pattern，跨数据集需要 recalibration。论文叙事：Re-DocRED 作为 robustness check 报告，承认 RSFT 增益\n    partially dataset-specific，但 evidence production capability 本身泛化良好。\n- name: EDCR Human Annotation Validation\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: 100 个样本人工标注验证：从 RSFT CED best 输出中采样 100 个 (triple, evidence) pairs，人工判断\n    evidence 是否真正支持对应 relation。计算 EDCR 与人工判断的 Spearman correlation。\n  expected_results:\n    n_annotated: 100\n    human_agreement_rate: 0.72\n    edcr_human_spearman_rho: 0.55\n    edcr_human_spearman_p: 0.001\n    edcr_human_pearson_r: 0.48\n    human_evi_f1_correlation: 0.35\n    inter_annotator_agreement_kappa: 0.65\n    annotation_categories:\n      fully_supported: 58\n      partially_supported: 22\n      not_supported: 12\n      ambiguous: 8\n    edcr_precision_at_high: 0.7\n    edcr_precision_at_low: 0.45\n  result_rationale: EDCR 与人工判断达到 moderate correlation（ρ=0.55）而非 strong correlation，原因：(1)\n    EDCR 基于 NLI entailment probability，但 NLI 模型对 DocRE 域的 evidence 关系理解有局限——某些 relation\n    types（如 temporal、geographic）的 evidence 需要多跳推理，NLI 模型会给出 neutral 判断，而人类会判为 supported；(2)\n    EDCR 的 contrastive design 比较 gold evidence vs distractor 的 NLI 差值，但人工标注是 absolute\n    judgment（是否支持），两种 operationalization 有 systematic gap；(3) per-relation analysis\n    已显示 EDCR 与 evi_f1 几乎正交（ρ=-0.064），说明 EDCR 捕捉的维度与传统 evidence quality 不同，人工标注可能更接近\n    evi_f1 的语义（表面匹配），导致 EDCR-human 相关度受限。高 EDCR 端（>0.8，病理模型）precision 达 0.70（识别 'bad\n    evidence' 较准），但低 EDCR 端（<0.5，good models）precision 仅 0.45——说明 EDCR 更擅长诊断极端病理案例，对\n    fine-grained quality ranking 能力有限。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: EDCR Human Validation Summary'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Spearman ρ (EDCR vs human)\n      - '0.55'\n      - Moderate positive correlation\n    - - p-value\n      - <0.001\n      - Statistically significant\n    - - Human agreement (fully/partially supported)\n      - 80%\n      - Evidence generally useful\n    - - EDCR precision at pathological range\n      - '0.70'\n      - Good diagnostic for failure modes\n    - - EDCR precision at healthy range\n      - '0.45'\n      - Limited fine-grained discrimination\n  - name: 'Table: Human Annotation Distribution'\n    columns:\n    - Category\n    - Count\n    - Proportion\n    rows:\n    - - Fully supported\n      - '58'\n      - 58%\n    - - Partially supported\n      - '22'\n      - 22%\n    - - Not supported\n      - '12'\n      - 12%\n    - - Ambiguous\n      - '8'\n      - 8%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: EDCR score vs human support rating (4-point scale), with regression\n    line and confidence band'\n  - 'Confusion matrix: EDCR binary prediction (threshold=0.7) vs human binary judgment\n    (supported vs not)'\n  analysis: ρ=0.55 支持 EDCR 作为有意义的诊断指标，但不足以声称 'validated automatic metric'。关键发现：EDCR\n    在方法级诊断（区分 catastrophic vs healthy models）的有效性远高于 sample 级 fine-grained ranking。论文需加\n    caveat：'EDCR demonstrates moderate correlation with human judgments (ρ=0.55, p<0.001),\n    providing useful method-level diagnostics while acknowledging limitations in instance-level\n    precision. Further large-scale validation is needed before EDCR can serve as a\n    standalone evaluation metric.' Claim 4 的 Layer 1（方法级）不受影响——EDCR vs rel_f1 的 ρ=-0.965\n    是纯数值关系，不依赖人工验证。Layer 2（per-relation 诊断）需要 qualified：'EDCR reveals relation-type\n    difficulty patterns that merit further human validation.'\n- name: NLI Model Ablation (DeBERTa-base vs large)\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 用 DeBERTa-v3-base 替代 DeBERTa-v3-large 作为 CED scorer，重新打分 RSFT candidates\n    并训练，对比 RSFT 质量差异。验证 NLI 模型能力对 CED scoring quality 的影响。\n  expected_results:\n    base_ced_discrimination_accuracy: 0.755\n    large_ced_discrimination_accuracy: 0.815\n    base_rsft_ign_f1: 44.1\n    large_rsft_ign_f1: 45.0\n    base_rsft_rel_f1: 0.448\n    large_rsft_rel_f1: 0.4569\n    base_rsft_evi_f1: 0.805\n    large_rsft_evi_f1: 0.8143\n    delta_ign_f1: -0.9\n    delta_rel_f1: -0.0089\n    base_selection_rate: 0.135\n    large_selection_rate: 0.124\n    base_mean_ced_score: 0.625\n    large_mean_ced_score: 0.668\n  result_rationale: DeBERTa-v3-base 比 large 参数少 60%（184M vs 434M），NLI accuracy 从 ~91%\n    降至 ~88%（MNLI benchmark）。这导致 CED scoring 的 discrimination accuracy 从 0.815 降至 0.755——base\n    模型在 subtle evidence distinctions（需要深层语义理解的 cases）上给出更多 false positives，selection\n    threshold 下 base 选出更多但质量更低的 samples（selection rate 略高 13.5% vs 12.4%）。传导至 RSFT\n    训练：base-scored 数据中混入更多 borderline/noisy samples，最终 RSFT 模型退化约 0.9pp Ign-F1。这个差距存在但不大（不足\n    1pp），原因是 CED 的 contrastive design 本身有 robustness——即使 absolute NLI scores 不准确，gold\n    vs distractor 的 relative ordering 在 base model 下仍大部分保持。结论：NLI model quality matters\n    but is not the dominant factor——CED 的 contrastive margin 设计提供了对 NLI model imperfection\n    的一定鲁棒性。这支持 Claim 3 的 'NLI-based scoring 是关键' 叙事（即使用 weaker NLI model 仍有效）。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: NLI Model Ablation'\n    columns:\n    - NLI Model\n    - Params\n    - CED Discrim. Acc\n    - RSFT Ign-F1\n    - RSFT rel_f1\n    - RSFT evi_f1\n    rows:\n    - - DeBERTa-v3-large\n      - 434M\n      - '0.815'\n      - '45.0'\n      - '0.4569'\n      - '0.8143'\n    - - DeBERTa-v3-base\n      - 184M\n      - '0.755'\n      - '44.1'\n      - '0.4480'\n      - '0.8050'\n    - - Δ (base - large)\n      - —\n      - '-0.060'\n      - -0.9pp\n      - '-0.0089'\n      - '-0.0093'\n    note: large 为 3-seed mean (CED RSFT s42/s44)，base 为 1-seed estimate\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: CED discrimination accuracy and downstream RSFT performance for base\n    vs large NLI model'\n  analysis: NLI model ablation 在 median 档下为 Claim 3 提供补充而非关键证据。base 模型仍能产出有效的 RSFT\n    训练数据（rel_f1=0.448 仍显著优于 SFT baseline 0.405），但优势缩减约 1pp。作为 P2 ablation 放入附录即可——主要结论是\n    CED 的 contrastive design 对 NLI model quality 有一定 tolerance，但 stronger NLI model\n    still helps。不影响核心 claims。\n- name: Post-hoc Evidence Retrieval Baseline (SFT + BM25)\n  plan_id: post_hoc_retrieval\n  description: 用 SFT no-evidence 模型抽取 relations，再用 BM25 从文档中 retrieve evidence sentences。对比\n    RSFT 端到端方案的 evidence 质量。验证 post-hoc retrieval 是否为更简单的替代方案。\n  expected_results:\n    posthoc_rel_f1: 0.4893\n    posthoc_ign_f1: 0.4736\n    posthoc_evi_f1_bm25: 0.74\n    posthoc_edcr: 0.58\n    rsft_best_evi_f1: 0.8156\n    rsft_best_rel_f1: 0.4683\n    delta_evi_f1_vs_rsft: -0.076\n    delta_rel_f1_vs_rsft: 0.021\n    bm25_recall_at_3: 0.82\n    bm25_precision_at_3: 0.55\n  result_rationale: Post-hoc retrieval 的 rel_f1 等于 SFT no-evidence（0.4893）因为 relation\n    extraction 与 evidence retrieval 完全解耦——这是其最大优势（无 evidence tax）也是最大弱点。BM25 evidence\n    retrieval 达到 evi_f1=0.74，原因：(1) DocRE 的 evidence sentences 通常包含 head/tail entity\n    mention，BM25 的 term matching 能有效定位这些句子；(2) 但 BM25 无法处理需要推理的 evidence（entity 未直接出现在\n    evidence sentence 中的 cases），这类约占 25-30%。evi_f1=0.74 vs RSFT 的 0.82——差距约 8pp，处于\n    median tier 定义的 '差距不够显著(<10pp)' 范围。这削弱了 RSFT 端到端方案的不可替代性叙事：一个简单的 two-stage pipeline（better\n    extraction + BM25 retrieval）在 rel_f1 上更高（+2.1pp，因无 evidence tax）且 evidence quality\n    差距有限。但 post-hoc 方案的 EDCR 为 0.58（高于 RSFT 的 0.64），说明 BM25 retrieved evidence 虽然\n    token overlap 高但 faithfulness 更差——它检索的是 'relevant' 而非 'supporting' sentences。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: End-to-end vs Post-hoc Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Approach\n    - rel_f1\n    - Evi-F1\n    - EDCR\n    - Total Latency\n    rows:\n    - - RSFT CED (end-to-end)\n      - '0.4683'\n      - '0.816'\n      - '0.639'\n      - 1x\n    - - SFT no-evi + BM25 (post-hoc)\n      - '0.4893'\n      - '0.740'\n      - '0.580'\n      - 1.2x\n    - - CED reranker (N=8)\n      - '0.4864'\n      - '0.819'\n      - '0.616'\n      - 8x\n    note: Post-hoc rel_f1 更高因为无 evidence generation burden\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Radar chart: end-to-end vs post-hoc on 4 axes (rel_f1, evi_f1, EDCR, efficiency)'\n  analysis: Post-hoc baseline 是 median 档下最具威胁的对比实验。它暴露了 RSFT 端到端方案的核心张力：为了 jointly\n    produce evidence 付出了 rel_f1 代价（-2.1pp vs no-evidence），获得的 evidence quality 优势仅\n    +7.6pp evi_f1。论文应对策略：(1) 强调 EDCR 差异——RSFT 的 evidence 更 faithful（EDCR 0.64 vs 0.58），不只是表面\n    overlap；(2) 指出 post-hoc approach 无法保证 evidence-relation consistency（retrieve 到的\n    evidence 可能支持文档中其他 relation 而非 predicted one）；(3) 将 comparison 框架为 'trade-off\n    analysis' 而非 'RSFT wins'——端到端方案在 faithfulness 上有优势，two-stage 在 extraction accuracy\n    上有优势，choice depends on application requirements。Claim 1 不再能声称端到端方案不可替代，需调整为 'one\n    effective approach with unique faithfulness properties'。\n","numLines":383,"startLine":1,"totalLines":383}}}
